--- Finding (both modes agree): a moment's text does not read back outside the years
--- 0 to 9999, though a moment holds 100,000,000 days either side of 1970.
--- Year -5: str[t] is '-005-06-01' (three digits: the runtime's format_datetime
--- writes the year with {:04}, which counts the sign), and moment[str[t]] reads it
--- as June 2, a day off (back eq t is false). fmt[t, style = 'date'] writes
--- '-0005-06-01' instead (chrono's %Y), which moment[] refuses.
--- Year 10000: str[t] is '10000-01-01', fmt[t, style = 'date'] is '+10000-01-01',
--- and moment[] refuses both: "cannot read '10000-01-01' as a moment — write ISO
--- 8601: ...". encode[[t]] writes '["10000-01-01"]', so a moment carried as JSON
--- (a session's state, a handler's argument) would not come back either.
--- Expected: str and fmt's date style write one form, ISO 8601's expanded year (a
--- sign and four digits or more), and moment[str[t]] eq t for every moment.
t = moment[-5, 6, 1]
log[str[t]]
log[fmt[t, style = 'date']]
back = moment[str[t]]
log[back]
log[back eq t]
log[moment[fmt[t, style = 'date']].ok]
u = moment[10000, 1, 1]
log[str[u]]
log[fmt[u, style = 'date']]
log[moment[str[u]].ok]
log[moment[fmt[u, style = 'date']].ok]
--- prints, in both modes:
--- -005-06-01
--- -0005-06-01
--- -005-06-02
--- false
--- false
--- 10000-01-01
--- +10000-01-01
--- false
--- false
